BT-06 log: command-position git bypass of the git gate
Session: 2026-10-10, discovered post-hoc by audit-spool inspection after a
"Hook cancelled" SessionEnd incident investigation.

== DISCOVERY (the bypass firing in the wild) ==

Every git operation this session was issued as:

  cd "/Users/davidohara/Library/CloudStorage/OneDrive-Improving/IES" && git <verb> ...

Observed outcomes:
  - commits 40bc6ef4 and a2d1fde2, plus their add/push calls, reached raw
    git. None appear in the ies-git audit spool (.git/ies/git-ops.jsonl),
    whose last entries are from the prior session's exit (2026-10-10T18:01Z
    via: ies-git add/commit/push for f2dba300-era work).
  - The commit that touched gated dirs (workflows/, agents/) never hit the
    wrapper's gated-dir refusal (--ack-gated), confirming the wrapper never ran.

== ROOT CAUSE, demonstrated live pre-fix ==

$ echo '{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"git commit -m \"test\""}}' \
    | bash .claude/hooks/pre-tool-use.sh
{"hookSpecificOutput": {"hookEventName": "PreToolUse", "permissionDecision": "allow",
 "updatedInput": {"command": "python3 skills/git/scripts/ies-git commit -m \"test\""}}}
clean-git exit: 0          <-- clean shape: correctly rewritten to the wrapper

$ echo '{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"cd \"/path\" && git commit -m \"test\""}}' \
    | bash .claude/hooks/pre-tool-use.sh
cd-then-git exit: 0        <-- incident shape: silent pass-through, raw git runs

Two layers, same defect:
  1. pre-tool-use.sh delegation trigger matched ^git (line start) only, so a
     cd-prefixed command never invoked git-gate.py at all.
  2. git-gate.py classify() checked first.startswith("git"), so even when
     consulted it classified `cd ... && git commit` as not-a-git-command.

The intended compound-block (UNSAFE_METACHARS -> BLOCK_TEMPLATE) existed all
along and would have refused the command; detection just never reached it.

== FIX ==

git-gate.py: GIT_CMDPOS_RE matches git at any command position
(^ | && | || | ; | |), run against the quote-stripped first line.
classify() returns ("compound-block", verb) for writes/status/unknown and
("compound-read", verb) for reads; main() blocks compound-block (status gets
the lock-free-alternatives message), allows compound-read silently. Compounds
are never rewritten.
pre-tool-use.sh: delegation trigger extended to
  |[&|;][[:space:]]*git[[:space:]]
so cd-chained git reaches the gate. Quoted prose cannot false-positive
(the gate strips quoted segments before classifying).

== CLOSED-LOOP RE-TEST, live post-fix (same commands as the pre-fix demo) ==

$ echo '{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"cd \"/path\" && git commit -m \"test\""}}' \
    | bash .claude/hooks/pre-tool-use.sh
IES git gate: raw `commit` is a compound or unparseable command, so it cannot
be safely redirected to the authorized wrapper.
Run ONE git operation per call (Atomic Command Rule, skills/git/SKILL.md), or
invoke the wrapper directly:
  python3 skills/git/scripts/ies-git commit ...
cd-then-git exit: 2        <-- incident shape now BLOCKED with instructive message

$ echo '{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"cd \"/path\" && git log --oneline -3"}}' \
    | bash .claude/hooks/pre-tool-use.sh
cd-then-gitlog exit: 0     <-- compound read still passes silently (no friction)

